course: dictionary
lesson: 478
title: A plant with a famous medicine
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a whole group of things, not just one. Artemisia is a group of plants with strong-smelling, often silvery leaves, such as wormwood, mugwort, sagebrush and tarragon.
explain: Context can show you when a word is a name. «For centuries women were often kept out of art academies; some, like Artemisia Gentileschi in 1600s Italy, still became famous.» The capital letter and the person's name after it tell you Artemisia is a woman's name here.
explain: Look at the clue words too. «Kept out» and «still became famous» go against each other, so «still» means "even so". Always check the words around a new word before you decide what it means.
fact: Artemisia is a noun for a group of plants, and its plural is artemisias.
fact: With a capital letter, Artemisia can be a woman's name, such as Artemisia Gentileschi, an Italian painter of the 1600s.
fact: Sweet wormwood (Artemisia annua) is the plant that the malaria medicine artemisinin is made from.
fact: Tu Youyou won a Nobel Prize in 2015 for discovering artemisinin.
fact: Plants in the artemisia group often have strong smells and silvery leaves.
exercise: Which of these is NOT in the artemisia group? | Wormwood | Tarragon | *Sunflower | Mugwort
exercise: Sweet wormwood is the plant that a famous medicine is made from. What is the medicine for? | Broken bones | *Malaria | Sore throats | Headaches
exercise: In «some, like Artemisia Gentileschi in 1600s Italy, still became famous», what is Artemisia? | A plant | A medicine | A country | *A woman's name
test: Which plant is the malaria medicine artemisinin made from? | *Sweet wormwood | Mugwort | Sagebrush | Tarragon
test: Who was Artemisia Gentileschi? | A plant in a garden | A kind of medicine | *An Italian painter of the 1600s | A famous scientist from 2015
exam: In «women were often kept out of art academies; some, like Artemisia Gentileschi, still became famous», which words show that "still" means "even so"? | *"kept out" and "still became famous" | "centuries" and "1600s" | "some" and "many others" | "art academies" and "Italy"
